> j the evoker S:10 D:13 C:14 I:18 W:9 Ch:11 Neutral AC:9
> +1 quaterstaff
> CoMR
> uncursed scrolls of genocide, remove curse and enchant armor

Read enchant armor on your cloak.
Save genocide for a tight situation, like being swarmed by soldier ants.
Remove curse will not be necessary in the very early game since you can
check the curse-status of items using your pet.

> spellbooks of force bolt and jumping

Use force bolt before you come into melee range.
Use jumping to escape in a tight situation. (Make sure you have enough
mana power to cast the spell.)

> uncursed pots of see invisible, gain ability and water

Use see invisible if you need it, e.g. are attacked by an invisible foe.
Try to bless gain ability before using it.
Look for an coaligned altar (or convert an unattended altar) to sacrifice
for Magicbane and converte your water to holy water by an altar-prayer.

> uncursed rings of fire r and +1 of protection

Wear your ring of protection, but watch your hunger status.

> wand of undead turning
> magic marker with 0:97

Write more scrolls of enchant armor and genocide when you have blanked
some useless scrolls (but be careful with fountain effects!) or found
scrolls of blank paper.

> Haven't played in a while and don't want to screw myself by making a
> quick decision... "Nethack isn't Quake..."
> 
> Last char died on mines level 8... I want this guy to go further :D
> Basicly wanted to know what are some of my options? I've read about
> genociding but haven't ever gotten far enough to get rid of litchs or
> anything like that... is it possible to curse the scroll and do the
> reverse genocide?

There are two problems with that; first, getting the scroll cursed, and
second, being able to fight the horde of tough monsters that you created.
I wouldn't reverse genocide early on, rather use the scroll to get rid
of a species that will kill you in some specific situation.

> drink the pots and wear the rings seems pretty
> obvious to me. enchant my cloak or wait for mithril?

Enchant your cloak, since it's likely that a wizard will keep the cloak
throughout the whole game. You will wear any body armor under your cloak.
If you find mithril armor, don't enchant it; it's temporary and typically
replaced by dragon armor.

